<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad Ali Jinnah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1876–1948</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Quaid-e-Azam</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad Ali Jinnah was the leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/all-india-muslim-league">All-India Muslim League</a> and the founder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>. A barrister born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karachi">Karachi</a>, he moved from Hindu-Muslim unity to demanding a separate Muslim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a>, set out in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahore-resolution">Lahore Resolution</a> of 1940. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">Dominion</a> of Pakistan was created on 14 August 1947 he became its first Governor-General, and he died in office in September 1948.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muhammad-ali-jinnah.jpg" alt="Muhammad Ali Jinnah" width="320" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jinnah1945c.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
